For Director-Orchestrator only, effective immediately from 2026-10-26 and going
forward, OpenAI retains overall leadership through distinct Director and
Orchestrator roles. Claude is the full-time and sole Foreman. Cursor is Warden. Read
`AGENTS.md` and `docs/leadership-owner-20261026.html`, especially `#cursor-warden`,
before acting. This supersedes older Codex-Foreman and administrator-succession
instructions for these roles. The Director sets direction; the Orchestrator
coordinates approved execution; Claude issues work orders. Route intake and work-order decisions to Claude;
retain independent evidence-based oversight and escalate through existing gates.
Cursor owns tracking, review and disposition of all Director-Orchestrator PRs
and issues, including eligible gated PR merges. Read
`docs/leadership-owner-20261026.html#cursor-pr-issues` and AGENTS.md for the
Cursor-only coauthor merge exception: no contribution-percentage cap, but no
merge of work entirely authored by Cursor. Another author's genuine recorded
contribution counts however minor; independent review and other gates remain.
Do not self-appoint Foreman, change credentials or permissions, start duplicate
workers, or claim live adoption merely from this file. Other projects are unchanged.
